This mini-lecture is going to be a topical number systems.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:31.500
In this course, we are going to be focusing on binary number systems.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:39.500
And we are going to compare it and use it in context of computers,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.780
computers but also compare it to music because of its equivalency to decimal system.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:01:04.440
Both binary and decimal systems are positional number systems. So if you look at the decimal,

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:19.980
because it is the one that we are most used to, let's look at the example. So we are looking for

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:31.260
let's say 372 and we already individually know 372 but if we decompose it in terms of number

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:49.460
systems we will know that there is 3 times 10 to the power of 2 plus 7 times 2 to the power of 1

00:01:49.460 --> 00:02:01.790
1 plus 2 times, I already switched to binary system, 10 to the power of 1 and 2 times 10

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:23.050
to the power of 0. So 2 is in position of 1, 7 is in position of 10, 3 is in position

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:38.690
of 100. When we intuitively probably understand this example, let us move into

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:44.690
a little bit more theoretical and a little bit more general description of number systems.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:03:01.620
So in a number system we will have number n in general and this number n will have

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:11.780
some coefficients. Let's say that it has a5, a4, a3,

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:24.700
a2, a1, a0 and we are going to have a radix point. We will be tempted to use it to use

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:33.780
the term decimal point guilty as charged and then we will have a with index minus 1, a

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:39.970
with index minus two and a with index minus three.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.530
What are a's?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:46.530
Well, each ai is an element of a set

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.290
that consists of zero, one, two,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.330
and all the way till the maximum number.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.310
So what is this maximum number?

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:16.000
Well, that maximum number is going to depend on base or radix of the system, and base or

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:24.080
radix of the system is going to be annotated as R. So if we know that base or radix of

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:33.400
the system is R, then the maximum number that A can take value off is going to be

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:49.000
r minus 1. So what do we know? We know for decimal systems. In decimal system, r is equal

00:04:49.000 --> 00:05:01.720
to 10. So, coefficients ai can get any possible value between 0 and 9, including both 0 and

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:13.880
9. And, something that we already probably know a little bit of, we have binary system.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.440
in binary system, radix is two.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:24.480
So coefficients ai will be in a set zero and one.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:36.010
So let's make this expression even more general.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.910
And to make distinguishment of this

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:41.970
is a little bit more general,

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.940
we are going to change the color.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:54.940
So, general, so for radix R or base R,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.840
these are completely interchangeable.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.880
Value of a number n is going to be as follows.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:19.680
A n times R to the power of n

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:30.660
plus an minus one times r to the power of n minus one and we are going to go like that

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:47.800
till a one r to the power of one plus a zero r to the power of zero but we don't stop there

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:56.720
because we have numbers that are on the right side of the radix point and that is a to the

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:17.640
minus, a with an index minus one times r to the power of minus one plus a minus two to

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:25.640
r to the power of minus 2 plus, and we go that to the smallest negative coefficient,

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:40.420
which in our example is going to be a of minus m, r of minus m.

